  "lossless_genome_and_all_event_record_spec": {
    "target_modules": [
      "crates/paper-artifacts/src/corpus.rs",
      "crates/crescent/src/jev.rs"
    ],
    "invariants": [
      "Birth-before-evaluation: every proposed birth receives a monotonic run-local birth ID before geometry decoding or FEM evaluation.",
      "Failed, geometrically rejected, and unscreened births are preserved in the event stream with explicit status tags (never silently dropped or zero-filled).",
      "Lossless 129-column genome+material preservation: all 128 f64 coordinates and the categorical material column are preserved byte-for-byte in bounded zstd segments (< 8 MiB per segment).",
      "Separated transport, source, and scientific content hashes: compressed segment sha256, decompressed CSV/JSONL sha256, and canonical scientific payload sha256 are recorded independently.",
      "per JR-R1 (SC-DEC-183N §2.1): receipt metadata validators (validate_gen800_population_accession, validate_newer_corpus_join, validate_historical_population_adapter) must be complemented by real byte-reading Rust decoders that verify manifest membership, compressed segment sha256, zstd decompressed payload sha256, 146-column / 129-gene+material widths, 195,456 unique local IDs per run, and 0..800 generation bounds."
    ]
  }
